      "definition": "(F) As used in this section, \"last chance agreement\" means an agreement signed by both an appointing authority and an officer or employee of the appointing authority that describes the type of behavior or circumstances that, if it occurs, will automatically lead to removal of the officer or employee without the right of appeal to the state personnel board of review or the appropriate commission.\n\nLast updated August 7, 2023 at 2:17 PM",
      "id": "124.34-last-chance-agreement",
      "normalized": "last chance agreement",
      "scope": "As used in this division, \"felony\" means any of the following:",
